---
import Entry from '../../layouts/Entry.astro';
import Note from '../../components/Note.astro';
import Plate from '../../components/Plate.astro';
import Specimen from '../../components/Specimen.astro';
---
<Entry
  slug="playscan"
  image="/media/playscan-poster.jpg"
  links={[{ href: 'https://github.com/EshaanDhavala/PlayScan', label: 'Code on GitHub' }]}
>
  <h2><span class="label">The question</span>Can a model call the play just by watching TV?</h2>
  <p>
    Play-type data usually comes from someone charting every snap by hand. I wanted to see whether a model
    could do it from the same broadcast feed fans watch: no tracking chips, no All-22 film.
  </p>

  <Plate fig="1" wide>
    <video slot="media" src="/media/playscan.mp4" poster="/media/playscan-poster.jpg" autoplay muted loop playsinline aria-label="Screen recording of PlayScan labeling a live NFL broadcast play with its predicted type and confidence"></video>
    PlayScan running live over a broadcast. The overlay shows the play number, the predicted type, and the
    model’s confidence.
  </Plate>

  <h2><span class="label">What I built</span>Frames in, play type out</h2>
  <Note>Labeling was the real project: every clip cut and tagged by hand.</Note>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Data:</strong> I cut and labeled <mark>1,174 clips</mark> from full game broadcasts myself (326 pass, 419 run, 429 special teams), with scripts to auto-segment plays and speed up tagging.</li>
    <li><strong>Model:</strong> each clip is sampled to 16 frames. A pretrained ResNet18 turns each frame into a feature vector, an LSTM reads them in order (a fake then a dropback looks different from a mesh then a handoff), and a linear head picks the class. Training uses inverse-frequency class weights.</li>
    <li><strong>Live mode:</strong> it watches a region of the screen, detects when motion starts and stops to find each snap, classifies it, and logs the probabilities.</li>
  </ul>

  <Specimen rows={[
    ['Held-out accuracy', '89%'],
    ['Labeled clips', '1,174'],
    ['Classes', 'run · pass · special teams'],
    ['Frames per play', '16'],
  ]} />

  <h2><span class="label">Next</span>What I’d do with more time</h2>
  <p>
    A temporal-attention head instead of the LSTM, better scene-cut handling around replays, and extra
    heads for formation and motion, which should also help the main task.
  </p>
</Entry>
